# Hostile audit — inactive-chamber residual conservation

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Audited source:** `research/target_c_inactive_chamber_residual_conservation.md`  
**Verdict:** PASS as a proof-only exact consequence of canonical Sections 67 and 77.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.

## 1. Chamber boundary counts

For a bounded nonquadrilateral face, the augmented boundary count is its degree. Its
boundary vertices are original source points and every boundary edge is a unit contact.
Thus Oler on boundary vertices plus assigned isolates gives `sigma_j>=k_j`.

For an outer pocket, canonical Section 67.6 explicitly defines the graph-boundary
count `k_P`, Euclidean perimeter `L_P`, and assigned population `z_P`, and proves

\[
 z_P\le A_P/a_0+L_P/2+1-k_P.
\]

This is exactly `sigma_P>=k_P`. The assignment convention for a source point lying on
an added hull side is already built into canonical (67.28); the new theorem does not
double count it.

The exact total count

\[
 K_{ch}=(4f+Q)+(b+2a-q)
\]

uses canonical (67.24) and the literal exceptional-face degree sum. No simple-boundary
replacement of the old occurrence-counted outer walk is made.

## 2. Algebra audit

Start from

\[
 \sum_j(\sigma_j-k_j)
 ={A_{ch}\over a_0}+{P_{ch}\over2}+s-Z_{ch}-K_{ch}.
\]

Insert

\[
 A_{ch}=A_F-a_0R_4-E_4,
 \quad Z_{ch}=N_F-m,
 \quad s=f+a,
\]

\[
 P_{ch}=4f+Q+b+2L_{add}-P_F,
\]

\[
 K_{ch}=4f+Q+b+2a-q,
 \quad m=R_4+f+q-k+1.
\]

After cancelling `R_4` and collecting terms, the remainder is

\[
 {A_F\over a_0}-N_F-{E_4\over a_0}
 +2q-k-{Q+b\over2}+L_{add}-{P_F\over2}-a+1.
\]

Canonical `Q+b=2(q-k)` reduces this to

\[
 {A_F\over a_0}-N_F-{E_4\over a_0}
 +q+L_{add}-a-{P_F\over2}+1.
\]

Canonical `P_F=q-a+L_add` then gives exactly

\[
 R_F={A_F\over a_0}+{P_F\over2}+1-N_F-{E_4\over a_0}.
\]

No asymptotic error is present.

## 3. Sign audit

Canonical Section 67.4 is

\[
 a_0N_F\le A_F+{a_0\over2}P_F+a_0-E_4.
\]

Dividing by `a_0` is precisely `R_F>=0`. This matches the chamber-by-chamber proof
that every residual `sigma_j-k_j` is nonnegative.

Thus the identity has two independent sign checks: local Oler and the global punctured
force-hull Oler inequality.

## 4. Capacity interpretation audit

For an internal exceptional face, the contact-wall theorem gives a globally safe
fixed-boundary replacement criterion. Oler gives only

\[
 M_\partial(C_j)-z_j\le r_j.
\]

Summing this over internal faces is valid and yields an upper bound by `R_F`.

No analogous globally safe capacity statement is asserted for an outer pocket, because
a subunit segment may cross its artificial hull chord. The residual identity includes
outer pockets only as an accounting statement.

Most importantly, the theorem never reverses

\[
 M_\partial-z\le r.
\]

`R_F` is an allowance, not a realized number of available packing slots.

## 5. Source/core scope

All counts use the full source population `N_F` and the canonical assignment of
contact-isolated points to chambers. No isolate is deleted from the theorem, and no
isolate is inserted into the Section-57 positive-core affine-kernel statement.

## 6. Exact frontier effect

Canonical Section 77 already gives `sum sigma_j=O(D)` and the boundary ledgers give
`K_ch=O(D)`, so `R_F=O(D)` is not a new order estimate. The new content is the exact
conservation law: after mandatory augmented-boundary credit is removed, every chamber
residual sums to one source-level scalar.

This blocks a common but invalid continuation in which several chamber Oler slacks are
treated as independent repacking budgets.

**Final verdict:** PASS. The result is useful bookkeeping and a structural reduction,
not an inactive-branch closure.
